                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "(Got this game via dev's submission to SteadyGiveaways.  Thanks!)\n\n[h1]It took less than 6 minutes for me to put this game down...[/h1]\n\n[i]Cars War[/i] is an overpriced (currently labeled at a price of $4) asset flip with 2 modes.  A singleplayer game about killing \"zombies\" (and by that, I mean glowing football players) and a multiplayer mode about destroying other player's cars (...if you find other players willing to compete against).\n\nWhat else is there to say?  Well, in the singleplayer mode, you get around 16 \"zombies\" that spawn and your health doesn't recover between rounds.  But how would you know this?  Your health doesn't show up anywhere on the screen!  Of course, even if you complete a round, you'll get an exact clone of the previous round you just finished.  Final nail in the coffin?  Well...your car is equipped with a mounted machine gun, that only fires once per click.  Have fun!\n\nSo, do I recommend this?  Not at all.  [i]Cars War[/i] is something that brings nothing new to the table whatsoever.  It's priced for $4 but brings nothing to the table that's remotely worth even that. This is particularly odd considering that this game is 2GB large.  I cannot recommend this for ANY price unless it's either for free or any price below $0.10.  Don't insult us with asset flips.  Oh, and Dev?  Fix your label-less achievements.\n\n0.1 / 10  Nothing new here.  Just another game for the trash bin.",
